(6323059, 934374, 48560, '<td valign="top">really good, Bear!<br/>the mood, the backwards glance by the bird, it all worked so well!<br/>congrats on the blue ^^</td>', 'really good, Bear!the mood, the backwards glance by the bird, it all worked so well!congrats on the blue ^^', '2011-02-20 21:32:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(6323245, 934374, 30861, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Aleema:</b></div><hr/><i> I agree with SEG how did u get it to look so sharp after all that croping? i am really curious. 9 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>5D is full frame  so you can do a serious crop and STILL have the resolution of APS-C. This was not too much of a crop from the area that would have been covered had a shot the 400mm on the 7D instead. It''s been my experience that the 5D cropped to match the 7D sensor is every bit as good an image as the uncropped 7D rendering.<br/> <br/>In other words, I can crop my 400mm to approximately 620mm with no sacrifice compared to an APS-C camera, though I would do better yet if I could mount an actual, 600mm lens :-)<br/> <br/>And it''s a VERY good lens, that 100-400mm, very sharp and clean.</td>', 'Originally posted by Aleema: I agree with SEG how did u get it to look so sharp after all that croping? i am really curious. 9   5D is full frame  so you can do a serious crop and STILL have the resolution of APS-C. This was not too much of a crop from the area that would have been covered had a shot the 400mm on the 7D instead. It''s been my experience that the 5D cropped to match the 7D sensor is every bit as good an image as the uncropped 7D rendering. In other words, I can crop my 400mm to approximately 620mm with no sacrifice compared to an APS-C camera, though I would do better yet if I could mount an actual, 600mm lens :-) And it''s a VERY good lens, that 100-400mm, very sharp and clean.', '2011-02-20 23:38:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(6324641, 934551, 96751, '<td valign="top">Love it when everything lines up, don''t you?  Marvelous image.  Very tender and intimate.  Congrats on the placement and the bling.</td>', 'Love it when everything lines up, don''t you?  Marvelous image.  Very tender and intimate.  Congrats on the placement and the bling.', '2011-02-21 11:56:10.000000', NULL, 0),
